# Performance & Smoothness

Focus on performance and smooth user experience in this React Native app. Use **Bad** vs **Good** patterns below.

## Navigation

- **Bad:** No animation or `animation: 'none'` — feels abrupt
- **Good:** Use `slide_from_right` (LTR) or `slide_from_left` (RTL), 200–300ms duration
- **Bad:** Disabled gestures — users expect swipe-back
- **Good:** `gestureEnabled: true`, `fullScreenGestureEnabled: true`
- **Good:** Use `presentation: 'card'` for standard screens

## Lists & Rendering

- **Bad:** `FlatList` with large lists — can jank
- **Good:** `@shopify/flash-list` with `estimatedItemSize`
- **Bad:** Inline `style={{ flex: 1 }}` or new objects in list item render — new ref every render, extra re-renders
- **Good:** `StyleSheet.create` outside component, or stable style refs
- **Bad:** Anonymous callback in render: `onPress={() => doSomething(id)}` — new function every render, child re-renders
- **Good:** `useCallback` or pass stable handler + data (e.g. `onPress={handler}` with `itemId` in item)
- **Good:** Memoize list items with `React.memo()`; use `getItemType` for heterogeneous lists

## State Management

- **Bad:** `const store = useStore()` or `useStore()` — subscribes to whole store, re-renders on any change
- **Good:** `useStore((s) => s.value)` — only re-render when `value` changes
- **Bad:** Storing derived values in state (e.g. `isRTL` from `language`) without deriving — can get out of sync
- **Good:** Derive in selector or `useMemo`: `const isRTL = useStore((s) => s.language === 'ar')`
- **Good:** Split stores by domain to reduce subscription scope

## Images & Assets

- **Bad:** Full-size images for thumbnails — memory and scroll jank
- **Good:** Resized/cached thumbnails, appropriate dimensions
- **Bad:** No loading/placeholder for images — layout shift, poor UX
- **Good:** Placeholder or skeleton while loading
- **Good:** Use SVG for icons when possible

## User Experience

- **Bad:** No feedback on tap (e.g. language switch) — user unsure if it worked
- **Good:** Toast, loading state, or visual feedback
- **Bad:** Blocking the UI for async work with no indicator
- **Good:** Show loading state; keep UI responsive
- **Bad:** Long lists with no virtualization
- **Good:** Use FlashList/virtualized list
